Modification (the only change from upstream 18.1.3, in src/Lexer.ts):
a fast path in the inline lexer (#tokenizeInlines) plus a findPlainChunkEnd
helper. A run of plain inline text — no character that can start a non-text
inline token (backslash, <, [, !, backtick, *, _, ~, &, @, www., ://, mailto:,
xmpp:, or a hard break), with email-aware handling so an address containing
`_` is still autolinked whole — is emitted directly as the single text token
marked's inline lexer would produce, without running the tokenizers or the
inline text regex. Every other run goes through marked's inline lexer
unchanged. The change is a pure speedup: it cannot alter any output.
